## Modifications — upstream copies edited by `scripts/patch-vendor-specifiers.mjs`

Apache-2.0 §4(b) requires modified files to carry a notice that they changed.
Both files below carry such a notice in their header; the rewrite is generated
by `scripts/patch-vendor-specifiers.mjs` and is idempotent.

| Vendored path | Upstream path | SHA-256 (upstream) | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| `playwright-core/src/tools/mcp/cdpRelay.ts` | `packages/playwright-core/src/tools/mcp/cdpRelay.ts` | `5f19dfb0034a2877029c36e5a4c665082ff27a1b0af22374f8f796f91d98078d` | 4 playwright-internal specifiers rewritten to package-relative paths |
| `playwright-core/src/tools/mcp/cdpRelayV2.ts` | `packages/playwright-core/src/tools/mcp/cdpRelayV2.ts` | `db32c68ffe422bfef9e477f23d062c79c79150ca9c5b3503618d26a7524e1556` | 1 playwright-internal specifier rewritten to a package-relative path |

The rewrite exists because upstream addresses its own helpers through
playwright-internal specifiers (`@isomorphic/manualPromise`, `@isomorphic/time`,
`@isomorphic/timeoutRunner`, `@utils/wsServer`) that are not registry packages
and were previously resolved through tsconfig `paths` + a bundler alias +
`JITI_TSCONFIG_PATHS`. None of those exists in an npm, managed, or Electron
install, so the plugin failed to load there. Package-relative specifiers
resolve in every install mode. **Relay behaviour is unchanged** — only the
import paths changed.

## Authored shims — NOT upstream

- `playwright-core/src/server/registry/index.ts` — replaces the ~60 KB
  upstream registry module. Only `registry.isChromiumAlias` /
  `registry.findExecutable` are reachable (from `cdpRelay.ts`'s
  `_openConnectPageInBrowser`, which this plugin bypasses in favour of the
  host `systemOpen` capability). Both throw
  `not supported — browser launch is supplied by relay-instance.ts`.
- `shims/wsServer.ts` — replaces upstream `packages/utils/wsServer.ts`.
  Upstream `CDPRelayServer` constructs a `WSServer` eagerly but only
  `listen()` binds a port. The transport is supplied by `relay-instance.ts`
  via `ctx.registerWsRoute`, so `listen()` throws and `close()` rejects with
  `not supported — transport is supplied by relay-instance.ts`.

